  "rationale": "Both answers are semantically valid, but the national split is materially overstated. Indonesian uses both \"tempat pensil\" and \"kotak pensil\"; Malaysian Malay uses both \"bekas pensel\" and \"kotak pensel\". The forms are transparent cognate equivalents, not a meaningful false-friend contrast. The card should present these as variety-associated preferences or common alternatives rather than sharply different words.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Correct. \"Pencil case\" denotes a small container or bag for pens, pencils, and related stationery.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/pencil-case"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: kotak pensil",
      "conclusion": "Valid Indonesian equivalent, but not demonstrably the sole or clearly dominant everyday form. \"Tempat pensil\" is also widely used for the same object.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://www.ikea.co.id/in/produk/mainan-dan-kreativitas/kreativitas/solfagel-art-50556346",
        "https://shopee.co.id/list/Tempat/Pensil"
      ],
      "evidence_limitation": "The available sources establish real Indonesian usage but do not provide a representative national frequency comparison between the two forms."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian Malay answer: bekas pensel",
      "conclusion": "Valid and clearly attested Malaysian Malay equivalent, but \"kotak pensel\" is also used for the same item.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://stationery.lazada.com.my/guide-to-choosing-pencil-cases-and-organizers-under-rm20-for-school-students-my/",
        "https://eperolehan2.mbip.gov.my/tender/bq/01kpgqbzkecewsycb9j370xs70",
        "https://www.lazada.com.my/videodetail/?video_id=30014050229"
      ],
      "evidence_limitation": "The sources show Malaysian usage and competing terminology but do not establish nationwide preference rankings."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Final relation and national split",
      "conclusion": "The relation \"different-common-word\" is too strong as currently presented. The answers differ in preferred lexical choice and spelling, but ordinary equivalents overlap across varieties: Indonesian \"tempat pensil\" and Malaysian \"kotak pensel\" are both attested, alongside the carded forms.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/pencil-case",
        "https://www.ikea.co.id/in/produk/mainan-dan-kreativitas/kreativitas/solfagel-art-50556346",
        "https://stationery.lazada.com.my/guide-to-choosing-pencil-cases-and-organizers-under-rm20-for-school-students-my/",
        "https://www.lazada.com.my/videodetail/?video_id=30014050229"
      ],
      "evidence_limitation": "Available evidence supports overlap and attestation, but not precise regional frequency or preference."
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No false-friend contrast is supported. \"Kotak/bekas/tempat\" transparently refer to a container or place for writing tools, and \"pensil/pensel\" is a regular orthographic variety difference. The empty contrast field is therefore not itself a factual error, though an explicit note that these are near-equivalent alternatives would reduce learner confusion.",
      "material_risk": false,
